### 1. SEARCH STRATEGY & SCOPE
Look for three Tiers of similarity:
- Tier 1 (Identical): Same biological question, same model organism, same intervention/methodology.
- Tier 2 (Highly Similar): Same intervention or mechanism but in a closely related model system (e.g., mouse vs. rat; a different but functionally identical cell line), or a slightly different technique answering the same question.
- Tier 3 (Conceptual Overlap): The conceptual framework or overall finding has been demonstrated elsewhere, even if the specific molecular target or tissue type differs slightly.

